WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.651
The five-ten K pathway clears a new device by showing substantial equivalence to one already on the market.

2
00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:12.918
Indications match. Technology matches. Performance matches. Safety matches.

3
00:00:12.933 --> 00:00:24.624
The framework was written for devices with fixed specifications. A I-enabled software has weights that change between releases. Substantial equivalence becomes ambiguous.

4
00:00:24.633 --> 00:00:32.324
Caventia pins the device to a specific model version, attaches the production performance evidence, and stabilizes the comparison.
